    "text": "Here's the implementation of the `split_words` function in Python:\n\n```\ndef split_words(txt):\n    if txt.count(',') == txt: \n        words = txt.split(',')\n    else txt:\n        words = txt.split()\n\n    return words\n    \n    # Return the number of odd words:\n    return 0\n\n\n```\n\nThis function splits the input string txt based on the presence of commas, if any. If not, it then splits it based on the presence of commas. Finally, it returns the number of words in the resulting list.\n\nYou can test this function with the provided examples to see how it works.",
